    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are prioritizing high-leverage top-of-the-order matchups today, with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the card at a 76.82 score. His favorable platoon alignment against Kremer and the added value of his leadoff spot make him an essential engine for our counting stats. **Jacob Wilson** also earns a strong recommendation (63.17); despite facing a competent arm in Peralta, his position in the three-hole combined with a favorable park factor significantly boosts his daily floor. **Andy Pages** (59.47) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.32) round out our most reliable contributors, both benefiting from high-order placement that offsets the moderate difficulty of their respective matchups.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, prioritizing efficiency to conserve game caps. **Wade Meckler** was the most difficult exclusion, landing at a 32.09 efficiency score. While his profile often provides speed, his negative platoon split against Gore and his placement at the bottom of the order rendered him unstartable today under our \"40-point floor\" mandate. Meanwhile, the injury status of **Jordan Westburg** continues to loom over our infield depth, and we remain without **Kyle Tucker**, who sits out today's rotation. With **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also sidelined due to his team's schedule, we are leaning heavily on the current active starters to drive our categories forward. \n\nWe are monitoring the matchup between **Jackson Merrill** and Henderson closely; while his 50.48 score is respectable, the elite 2.82 xERA of the opposing starter presents a genuine risk of a sub-optimal outcome. We are keeping a close watch on **Drake Baldwin**, whose 53.73 score is buoyed by leadoff duties but suppressed by a mediocre SP matchup. Given the extreme scarcity of stolen bases in this league, we are keeping a sharp eye on any late-inning defensive substitutions that could potentially involve **Nasim Nunez** or **Luis Lara** if the game scripts turn unfavorable for our primary starters.",
